Fillets: the OnSame end of a rounding wider than the face it ends against,
whose ball rolls on that face's edge with the face beyond, up to the vertex
(mitcad#236).

The case: a rod with a ridge along part of it (a cylinder of radius 2.5
whose axis lies on the rod's surface), the ridge's end face a lens 2.5
high; the lens's edge with the rod rounded with 5. The ball touches the rod
and rolls on the lens's other edge (Er, the arc where the lens meets the
ridge's side, the face B beyond Er); Er runs from one end vertex of the
spine to the other, and at both ends the edges are in the OnSame state.
Past each end the ball rolls on until it comes tangent to the ridge's side
(its surface prolonged past the lens), where the walk stops. The bodies
stored in the .f3d files cut the blend there with the ridge's side: from
that point on Er to the point where the rod's contact meets the ridge's
side, the ridge's edges with the rod prolonged up to it, the lens and Er
gone. OCCT took the face across Er (the lens) for the face at the end and
failed ("bouchon non ecrit", or "no point on arc" where no end point lay
on an edge).

- ChFi3d_RolledEndOnItsFace: at an OnSame end, a SurfData rolling on side
  s on an edge Er of its face B that holds the corner's vertex, whose ball
  at the end is tangent to B (the blend's normal along B's normal within
  0.05 rad at the contact): Er's point there is found.
- PerformOneCorner, OnSame: for such an end the face at the end is B
  itself, Er the arc, the other side's contact is intersected with B's
  surface as at any OnSame end (IntersUpdateOnSame) and B's edge at the
  vertex is prolonged to it; the point on Er is the end of the cap. Its
  transition, for the cap's orientation on B, is the vertex's orientation
  on Er; once the cap is stored it becomes EXTERNAL, so that Er goes from
  B on both sides (the blend's contact takes its place along the blend,
  B grows over it past the cap).

Upstream: new.
